  "text": "DONE. Both `xpm_fifo_async` instances in `rtl/fir32_core.sv` set `ECC_MODE(0)`, an integer. The real XPM takes a string, and Vivado read the 0 as ECC enabled. It then rejected the 16-bit write width, since ECC needs a multiple of 64. That error stopped elaboration of the FIFOs, the core and `fir32_top`.\n\n- **`rtl/fir32_core.sv`:** both FIFO instances (`u_in_fifo`, `u_out_fifo`) now use `.ECC_MODE(\"no_ecc\")`.\n- **`rtl/xilinx_sim_stubs.sv`:** the simulation stand-in for `xpm_fifo_async` now declares `ECC_MODE` as `parameter string ECC_MODE = \"no_ecc\"`, so the stand-in matches the real module.\n\n`fda_lint` passes after both edits. I did not re-run the Vivado build, `fda_simulate`, `fda_gates` or `fda_check`, so the synthesis fix is untested."
